facts:[
["Which three preparation steps open the neonatal algorithm before birth?","Antenatal counseling, team briefing, equipment check","Cord clamping, suctioning, intubation","Apgar scoring, weighing, vitamin K","Team briefing"],
["Which three questions are asked right after birth?","Term gestation? Good tone? Breathing or crying?","Pink color? Reflexes? Heart rate over 140?","Normal weight? Normal glucose? Normal temperature?","Breathing or crying?"],
["A term newborn has good tone and is crying. What does the algorithm direct?","Skin to skin with parent, routine care, maintain normal temperature, ongoing evaluation","Ventilate and apply a pulse oximeter","Dry, position, and begin chest compressions","Skin to skin with parent"],
["What are the initial steps when a newborn is not term, has poor tone, or is not breathing or crying?","Warm and maintain normal temperature, dry, position, stimulate and clear airway if needed","Intubate, give 100% oxygen, place a UVC","Start chest compressions and give epinephrine","Stimulate and clear airway if needed"],
["After the initial steps, which findings lead to ventilation?","Apnea or gasping, or HR <100/min","Crying with HR above 140/min","Any saturation below 95%","Apnea or gasping?"],
["How long does the AHA figure bracket from the cord management plan to starting ventilation?","1 minute","5 minutes","10 minutes","1 minute"],
["The newborn is being ventilated and HR is still <100/min. What comes next?","Ventilation corrective steps, consider intubation or laryngeal mask, cardiac monitor","Epinephrine by UVC or IO","Stop ventilation and observe","Ventilation corrective steps"],
["Which heart rate triggers chest compressions in the neonatal algorithm?","HR <60/min","HR <100/min","HR <80/min","HR <60/min?"],
["How are neonatal chest compressions coordinated with ventilation?","3:1","15:2","30:2","Coordinate 3:1 with ventilation"],
["What oxygen concentration is listed when neonatal chest compressions begin?","100% oxygen","21% oxygen (room air)","40% oxygen","100% oxygen"],
["Which vascular access routes does the neonatal algorithm list?","UVC or IO","Peripheral IV only","Central line through the neck","UVC or IO"],
["HR stays <60/min despite coordinated compressions and ventilation. What is given, and how often?","UVC or IO epinephrine every 3-5 minutes","Atropine every 10 minutes","Amiodarone once","UVC or IO epinephrine every 3-5 minutes"],
["If the newborn HR remains <60/min, which two problems does the algorithm say to consider?","Hypovolemia and pneumothorax","Hypoglycemia and seizures","Hypertension and fever","consider pneumothorax"],
["Target oxygen saturation at 2 minutes of life?","65%-70%","85%-95%","90%-98%","65%-70%"],
["Target oxygen saturation at 5 minutes of life?","80%-85%","65%-70%","95%-100%","80%-85%"],
["Target oxygen saturation at 10 minutes of life?","85%-95%","70%-75%","98%-100%","85%-95%"],
["A breathing newborn with HR at least 100/min has labored breathing or persistent cyanosis. What does the algorithm list?","Pulse oximeter, oxygen if needed, consider CPAP","Chest compressions 3:1","Epinephrine every 3-5 minutes","Consider CPAP"]],
cases:[
["A term baby is delivered, cries right away, and flexes all four limbs.","Skin to skin with parent and routine care","Dry, stimulate, and start ventilation","Place a pulse oximeter and start oxygen","Yes to term gestation, good tone, and breathing or crying leads to skin to skin, routine care, normal temperature, and ongoing evaluation."],
["After warming, drying, positioning, and stimulation, a newborn is gasping with HR 80/min.","Ventilate, apply a pulse oximeter, consider a cardiac monitor","Start chest compressions 3:1","Give UVC epinephrine","Apnea or gasping, or HR <100/min, leads to ventilation, pulse oximeter, and considering a cardiac monitor."],
["After ventilation corrective steps the newborn HR is 50/min.","Intubate or laryngeal mask, chest compressions coordinated 3:1, 100% oxygen, UVC or IO","Continue the same ventilation for 5 more minutes","Give epinephrine before any compressions","HR <60/min after corrective steps leads to an advanced airway, compressions coordinated 3:1 with ventilation, 100% oxygen, and UVC or IO access."],
["At 3 minutes of life, a ventilated newborn has HR 120/min and SpO2 72%.","The saturation is within the 3-minute target of 70%-75%","The saturation is dangerously low; give 100% oxygen and compress","The saturation is too high; stop all support","The table lists 70%-75% at 3 minutes. Targets rise gradually to 85%-95% at 10 minutes."],
["HR is 45/min after compressions coordinated with ventilation on 100% oxygen. A UVC is in place.","UVC or IO epinephrine every 3-5 minutes","Stop compressions and reassess in 5 minutes","Change the ratio to 15:2","HR <60/min at this point leads to epinephrine every 3-5 minutes; if HR remains <60/min, consider hypovolemia and pneumothorax."],
["After 30 seconds of effective ventilation the newborn HR rises to 130/min.","Postresuscitation care, communicate with family, team debriefing","Start chest compressions","Give epinephrine","HR is no longer <100/min, so the algorithm moves to postresuscitation care, communicating with family, and team debriefing."]],
