facts:[
["Pediatric BLS: how long may you take to check breathing and pulse together?","No more than 10 seconds","At least 30 seconds","A full minute","Is pulse definitely felt within 10 seconds?"],
["A child has a pulse but abnormal breathing. How often are breaths given?","1 breath every 2-3 seconds (20-30 breaths/min)","1 breath every 6 seconds (10 breaths/min)","1 breath every 10 seconds (6 breaths/min)","1 breath every 2-3 seconds (20-30 breaths/min)"],
["While supporting a child's ventilation, when is the pulse rate assessed?","After 2 minutes, then every 2 minutes","Every 10 seconds","Only when advanced care arrives","Assess pulse rate after 2 minutes."],
["Which heart rate, with poor perfusion despite oxygenation and ventilation, means start CPR in a child?","HR <60/min","HR <100/min","HR <40/min","HR <60/min with signs of poor perfusion despite oxygenation and ventilation?"],
["One rescuer, infant or child: which compression-to-breath cycle?","30 compressions and 2 breaths","15 compressions and 2 breaths","3 compressions and 1 breath","Perform cycles of 30 compressions and 2 breaths."],
["A second rescuer arrives to help with a child in arrest. Which cycle now?","15 compressions and 2 breaths","30 compressions and 2 breaths","5 compressions and 1 breath","perform cycles of 15 compressions and 2 breaths"],
["You are alone and witness a child's sudden collapse. What comes before CPR?","Activate the emergency response system and retrieve the AED/defibrillator to use immediately","Give 2 minutes of CPR before calling","Give naloxone","Retrieve AED/defibrillator and use immediately."],
["You are alone, the collapse was not witnessed, and you have started CPR. When do you leave to activate and get the AED?","After 2 minutes, if still alone","Immediately, before any CPR","After 10 minutes","After 2 minutes, if still alone, activate emergency response system"],
["Pediatric BLS: after a shock, what happens next?","Resume CPR immediately for 2 minutes","Check the pulse for 30 seconds","Give 3 stacked shocks","Give 1 shock. Resume CPR immediately for 2 minutes"],
["Pediatric BLS: the rhythm is nonshockable. What now?","Resume CPR immediately for 2 minutes","Stop CPR and wait for help","Deliver a shock anyway","Resume CPR immediately for 2 minutes"],
["How long do pediatric BLS rescuers continue?","Until PALS professionals take over or the infant or child starts to move","For exactly 10 minutes","Until the first shock is delivered","Continue until PALS professionals take over or the infant or child starts to move."],
["A child with a pulse and abnormal breathing may have an opioid overdose. What does the algorithm add?","Administer an opioid antagonist (eg, naloxone) if available","Give epinephrine","Give abdominal thrusts","administer opioid antagonist (eg, naloxone) if available"],
["Which patients does the pediatric BLS algorithm cover?","Infants to puberty","Newborns in the delivery room only","Anyone under 21 years","Infants to Puberty"]],
cases:[
["You are alone. A 6-year-old is unresponsive, gasping, with no pulse felt in 10 seconds. Nobody saw what happened.","Start CPR with cycles of 30 compressions and 2 breaths","Leave to find an AED before any CPR","Give breaths only, 1 every 2-3 seconds","Unwitnessed and alone: start CPR at 30:2, then activate the emergency response system and retrieve the AED after 2 minutes if still alone."],
["You are alone at a ball field. A 10-year-old suddenly collapses in front of you: unresponsive, no breathing, no pulse.","Activate the emergency response system, retrieve the AED/defibrillator and use it immediately","Give 2 minutes of CPR before calling","Open the airway and give breaths only","A witnessed sudden collapse sends a lone rescuer to activate and retrieve the AED/defibrillator and use it immediately, then CPR."],
["An infant is breathing abnormally. You definitely feel a pulse of 90/min.","Support ventilation: open and reposition the airway, 1 breath every 2-3 seconds","Start chest compressions","Monitor only until advanced care arrives","Abnormal breathing with a pulse leads to supported ventilation at 1 breath every 2-3 seconds, with a pulse check after 2 minutes."],
["After 2 minutes of rescue breaths, a toddler's HR is 50/min with mottled skin and weak pulses.","Start CPR","Continue breaths only and recheck in 2 minutes","Stop and monitor","HR <60/min with signs of poor perfusion despite oxygenation and ventilation moves to CPR."],
["Two rescuers are doing CPR on a 4-year-old. The AED says no shock advised.","Resume CPR immediately for 2 minutes at 15:2","Check the pulse for a minute","Remove the pads and stop","Nonshockable: resume CPR immediately for 2 minutes until the AED prompts a rhythm check. Two rescuers use 15:2."],
["A child is unresponsive, breathing normally, with a definite pulse.","Monitor until advanced care arrives","Start CPR 30:2","Give rescue breaths every 2-3 seconds","Normal breathing with a pulse felt: monitor until advanced care arrives."]],
